Removes the re-evaluation from `FolderState::take_one` (§7.3, draft 64):
a received deletion deferred because its directory held a file a user
rule ignores is no longer wanted again when a scan or the watcher next
observes the directory, so once the user takes the file away nothing
tries the deletion again, and the directory stays on this machine while
every other has deleted it. In the simulator a peer re-creating the
directory nearly always replaces the held want first: no seed in 0 to
9,999 fails with this patch, and one in 2,000 at ten times the rate, so
the rule's unit tests stand in.

test: delocal-engine folder::tests::a_deletion_held_by_ignored_files_is_tried_again_when_the_directory_is_next_seen
test: delocal-engine folder::tests::a_deletion_above_one_held_by_ignored_files_waits_for_it_observably
test: delocal-sim sim::tests::directories_held_by_an_ignored_file_are_left_out_of_i1_and_i3

